# From the copy that was bootstrap/examples/assume-method-before-type.moss (removed; its
# oracle verdicts are the old Rocq oracle's, historical):
# RecvTy reads no type symbol out of force as a nominal (AUDIT-CHANGES #59;
# D20; criteria section 6, fidelity). The method item T.m is listed before
# the type T, so while T.m is read, T is not in force.
# Audit before: accepts (RecvTy's fallback read T.m's receiver as the
# nominal `TNom T []`; argued). Audit now: rejects (RecvTy asks
# `kind_sym W T <> Some DKType` there, so IEMeth does not apply; argued).
# Oracle (moss_m2): rejects ("type `T` is not available in the context here").
# Native (ob-family moss, seed 1h1710x0): accepts (exit 0), a native bug
# (E41): it reads the list as a set here, while it rejects `assume f, T` with
# f mentioning T, and tests/errors/assume_method_before_type_use.moss.
type T;
fn .m(): This;
# E41 (AUDIT-CHANGES #59, D20): `T.m`'s receiver is the type `T` in force,
# and `T` is listed after it.
assume T.m, T { fn g() {} }
fn main() {}
